      "problem": "Compute $P(1<X\\le 5)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{18}x,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X\\le 5) & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{18}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{36}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
